  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "高分子結構與物性",
    "sub_ename": "STRUCTURE AND PROPERTIES OF POLYMERS",
    "describe_ch": "本課程將探討半導體製程中用到的高分子光阻結構，藉由光學曝光和顯影的物理原理，完整介紹半導體軟物質材料科學的實務應用，旨在了解各高分子結構與物性間之關係，使高分子型態、結構之基本理論及黏彈性質獲得充分解析",
    "describe_eh": "This course will explore the photoresist structure (i.e., photocurable polymer) used in semiconductor processes, and fully introduce the practical application of semiconductor from soft material science, through the physical principles of optical exposure and development. The aim is to understand the relationship between various polymer structures and physical properties, and to elucidate the basic theories and viscoelastic properties of polymer morphology and structure.",
